# The `caos-test` tool (SPEC, "Tools"): the dev/test-stack worker image with
# this directory's script curried onto it, plus the `help` an agent registers
# it by. It moved out of caos-tools/ into std/ so the agent harness can DEPend on
# it and register it ALWAYS — the tool comes from the harness's own version, not
# from the tree under test (design/flake-inputs.md, "the tui").
#
# The docs are a HERE-STRING, so they live here rather than in the script — and
# a `.caos-expr` is STRIPPED from the tree it is evaluated against, so editing
# them re-keys this tool's arg tree and nothing it builds. That split is why
# `@param [test-salt]` can be reworded without re-running a single test.
HELP=<<END
Build the caos test stack image from the tree and run the whole test suite — the
unit tests and every tests/<name> integration suite — as cached jobs: an
unchanged test never re-runs. Returns the report: a line per test with its
time and the hash of its record, the last few lines of every failing test,
and a pass/fail banner. Pass a record's hash to `caos-test-result` for that test's
full output or its inner-stack logs. Nothing is handed in from the host: the
stack under test is compiled from these sources, inside workers. This tool is
specific to the caos codebase; run in any other tree it reports cleanly that
there is nothing for it to test.
@param [test-salt] Re-run every test while leaving the build a cache hit — any fresh value (e.g. $(date --iso=s)) re-keys the tests and nothing else.
@param [only] Run only these tests — a space-separated list of tests/<name> directories.
END
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/test-stack --worker1:@=worker.sh --help=$HELP
